# https://si-digital-framework.org/SI#MeasurementUnit
<https://si-digital-framework.org/SI#MeasurementUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://si-digital-framework.org/SI#MeasurementUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Measurement unit defining the magnitude of the quantity in respect to the value.\nsi:MeasurementUnit class is reused"@en .
<https://si-digital-framework.org/SI#MeasurementUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Unit of measurement"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprint> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (25)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Carbon footprint\nmeans the sum of greenhouse gas emissions and greenhouse gas removals in a product system, expressed as CO equivalents and based on a life cycle assessment using the single impact category\nof climate change. (ESPR Art 2 25))\n\nThis class description needs to be extended/specialised according to the corresponding delegated acts or/and industry standards."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Carbon footprint"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#CircularEconomyIndicator
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CircularEconomyIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CircularEconomyIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#QuantitativeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CircularEconomyIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Circular Economy indicators are measures for relevant monitoring the transition to a circular economy and to measure the effects of new policy and trends.\n\nThis class description needs to be extended/specialised according to the corresponding delegated acts or/and industry standards."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CircularEconomyIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Circular Economy Indicator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#CircularEconomyIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://environment.ec.europa.eu/strategy/circular-economy-action-plan_en> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#ClassificationCode
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ClassificationCode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ClassificationCode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A classification code from some product classification scheme ."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ClassificationCode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ClassificationCode"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConcentrationOfSubstanceOfConcern
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConcentrationOfSubstanceOfConcern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConcentrationOfSubstanceOfConcern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#QuantitativeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConcentrationOfSubstanceOfConcern> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 7(5)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConcentrationOfSubstanceOfConcern> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConcentrationOfSubstanceOfConcern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The concentration of the substances of concern, at the level of the product, its relevant components, or spare parts ESPR Art 7(5)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConcentrationOfSubstanceOfConcern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Concentration of the substance of concern"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (28)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Digital Product Passport (DPP) means a set of data specific to a product that includes the information specified in the applicable\ndelegated act adopted pursuant to Article 4 and that is accessible via electronic means through a data carrier in accordance with Chapter III. (ESPR Art 2 (28))"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Digital Product Passport (DPP)"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#DigitalInstruction
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DigitalInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DigitalInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#DocumentFormattedProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DigitalInstruction> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 27(7)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DigitalInstruction> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DigitalInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Digital instructions\nmean instructions in digital format concerning the product (‘digital instructions’) in a language that can be easily understood. ESPR Art 27(7)\nDigital instructions are ensured by manufacturers. These should also ensured by importers. (ESPR Art 29(4))\n\nThis class can be extended/specialised according to delegated acts or industry standards."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DigitalInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "DigitalInstruction"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#DocumentFormattedProperty
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DocumentFormattedProperty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DocumentFormattedProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Property> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DocumentFormattedProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The document class describes the semantic representation of any instance of a document that might be required to be included into a digital product passport instance."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#DocumentFormattedProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Document"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#QualityIndicator> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (22)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Durability\nmeans the ability of a product to maintain over time its function and performance under specified conditions of use, maintenance and repair. (ESPR Art 2 (22))\n\nThis class description needs to be extended/specialised according to the corresponding delegated acts or/and industry standards."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Durability"@en .
