# https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#QualityIndicator> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Art 2 (16)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reliability\nmeans the probability that a product functions as required under given conditions for a given\nduration without an occurrence which results in a primary or secondary function of the product no\nlonger being performed. (ESPR Art 2 (16))\n\nReliability is usually expressed in terms of mean time between failures (MTBF), which is the average length of time that a device will operate without failure.\n\nThis class description needs to be extended/specialised according to the corresponding delegated acts or/and industry standards."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reliability"@en .
